#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:0
msgid ""
"Enable TPM-backed full disk encryption when you install Ubuntu Desktop to "
"protect your data with your computer's security chip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:7
msgid "Topics: Installation Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:11
msgid "Encrypt your disk with TPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:13
msgid ""
"Hardware-backed disk encryption protects the data on your disk using the "
"Trusted Platform Module (TPM) chip. It encrypts your Ubuntu installation and "
"your whole disk. Compared to traditional encryption methods such as LUKS, "
"hardware-backed disk encryption can provide more convenience or more "
"security, depending on your configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:15
msgid ""
"To learn how this encryption works, see {ref}`hardware-backed-disk-"
"encryption`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:19
msgid "Enable the encryption during installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:21
msgid ""
"You can enable hardware-backed encryption when you install Ubuntu Desktop. "
"You cannot enable or disable it after installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:23
msgid "To install Ubuntu with hardware-backed encryption:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:25
msgid ""
"Follow the instructions in {ref}`install-ubuntu-desktop` until {guilabel}"
"`Disk setup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:27
msgid ""
"On the {guilabel}`Disk setup` screen, select {menuselection}`Erase disk and "
"install Ubuntu --> Use hardware-backed disk encryption`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:30
msgid ""
"**Back up your data.** In this setup, Ubuntu overwrites your whole disk. All "
"files will be deleted on the device where you're installing Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:33
msgid "Check if the installer reports any errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:35
msgid ""
"Your system might not support all the required security features. In that "
"case, the installer doesn't allow you to proceed with TPM/FDE, or it "
"requires that you set a PIN or a passphrase. For more information, refer to "
"{ref}`hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:37
msgid ""
"In some cases, your system isn't configured for TPM/FDE but it's possible to "
"reconfigure it. The Ubuntu installer suggests automated or manual actions to "
"resolve this. Some actions might require you to reboot the system to apply "
"the modifications in the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:39
msgid ""
"On the {guilabel}`Create your account` screen, set a secure password for all "
"user accounts. Without an encryption passphrase, your data is only as safe "
"as the weakest of the user passwords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:41
msgid ""
"When the installation is done, the installer shows your recovery key for "
"your encrypted disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:43
msgid ""
"You can save the recovery key as a text file on another USB stick. You can "
"also load the QR code with your phone or take a photo of the screen showing "
"the recovery key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:45
msgid "**Store it somewhere safe**, such as in a password manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:48
msgid ""
"If you lose your recovery key, you might lose access to your data in certain "
"scenarios. While you're logged in, replace the existing recovery key as soon "
"as possible. See {ref}`tpm-fde-get-a-new-recovery-key`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:51
msgid ""
"After starting your new Ubuntu Desktop system, you can {ref}`configure a "
"disk encryption PIN or passphrase <tpm-fde-set-passphrase>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:53
msgid "Configure the encryption after installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/encrypt-your-disk-with-tpm.md:55
msgid "Refer to {ref}`configure-hardware-backed-disk-encryption`."
msgstr ""
